  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": "B00",
      "narration_text": "Hi, my name is Ushasvi Rachel, and this video is about why machine-learning datasets are split into training, validation, and test sets.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 9,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "drawon",
        "visual_intent": "Presenter introduction and three-role preview.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "intro"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B00.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B00.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.77,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B00.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "narration_text": "If a model performs well on the data it learned from, does that mean it will perform well on new data? Not necessarily. Training results alone do not show how well the model generalizes.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "divergence",
        "visual_intent": "Training performance versus generalization question.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "question"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.56,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "narration_text": "That is why data is split into separate roles. Training supports learning. Validation supports modeling choices. Testing provides a final evaluation of the selected workflow.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "cards",
        "visual_intent": "Dataset grid and three stacked roles.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "roles"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.65,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "narration_text": "The training set fits the model. From those examples, the model learns parameters, patterns, or decision boundaries. Train means learn.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 10,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "flow",
        "visual_intent": "Training examples flowing into learned model.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "training"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.7,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "narration_text": "Validation helps select hyperparameters, compare models, tune thresholds, or use early stopping without consuming the final test set. Not every workflow uses one fixed validation split; cross-validation may be used.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 15,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "cards",
        "visual_intent": "Validation choice cards and cross-validation caveat.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "validation"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.83,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "narration_text": "The test set is the final check on data that did not fit the model or repeatedly guide selection. Test means evaluate the chosen workflow—not guarantee future production performance.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "threshold",
        "visual_intent": "Protected test-set definition.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "test"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.69,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "narration_text": "Training and validation can form an improvement loop. The test set stays outside it. If test results repeatedly drive modeling decisions, the workflow adapts to that test set, so it is no longer a clean check on unseen data.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "branch",
        "visual_intent": "Train-validation loop beside protected test set.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "reuse"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.87,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "narration_text": "Training performance measures behavior on learned-from examples. Generalization asks about new observations. Overfitting can produce excellent training results while learning patterns that do not transfer.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "divergence",
        "visual_intent": "Training and generalization comparison with brief overfitting warning.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "generalization"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B07.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 12.91,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "narration_text": "There is no universally correct split percentage. The right approach depends on dataset size, the task, temporal structure, class imbalance, and the evaluation strategy.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "cards",
        "visual_intent": "Factors affecting split design and no-universal-percentage warning.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "depends"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B08.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.26,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "narration_text": "Time-series data needs special care. Randomly mixing future and past may create an unrealistic evaluation. For temporal prediction, training and evaluation should generally respect time order.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "timeline",
        "visual_intent": "Past-to-future temporal split.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "time"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B09.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.4,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "narration_text": "Repeated records from the same person, patient, customer, device, or SKU may need to stay together, depending on the task. Otherwise closely related records can cross the split. Poor splitting can leak information unavailable at deployment.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "groups",
        "visual_intent": "Grouped-record examples and leakage boundary.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "groups"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B10.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.13,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "narration_text": "Cross-validation repeatedly rotates which observations are used for training and validation. It can help model selection when data is limited, but it does not solve every evaluation problem or remove the need for a careful final check.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "rotate",
        "visual_intent": "Four rotating training and validation folds.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "cv"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B11.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-17T14:17:00-04:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.89,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:DataSplitsVertical",
        "at": "2026-10-17T14:24:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "narration_text": "Training data teaches the model, validation data helps us make modeling choices, and test data helps us evaluate whether those choices generalize to unseen examples.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "cards",
        "visual_intent": "Exact final three-role takeaway.",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "DataSplitsVertical",
          "props": {
            "kind": "takeaway"
          },
          "rendered": {
